I am going home in an auto.
The morning weather is very pleasant.
The auto stops near my flat.
There is a small vegetable shop near the flat.
I go into that shop.
I want fresh vegetables.
There are many vegetables in the shop.
I see tomatoes, carrots, and onions there.
I like tomatoes very much.
I point to the red tomatoes.
I speak to the shopkeeper.
"I want tomatoes," I say.
He smiles and takes a basket.
Then I point to the carrots.
"I want carrots and onions," I tell him.
He puts everything in the basket.
These are very good vegetables.
I am happy.
